{"verdict":"approved","issues":[{"severity":"minor","file":"test/fares.test.ts","line":1,"description":"Verification criterion 'fareFor returns 350 when called with a rider aged 64 who does not hold a pass' has no dedicated test. The existing base-fare test uses age 30, so a regression where the senior concession wrongly starts at age 64 would leave all 5 tests passing. Per blocker discipline this is not a blocker (additional tests beyond ticket scope), but it is a recorded coverage gap.","suggestedFix":"Optionally add an it block: expect(fareFor({ age: 64, hasPass: false })).toBe(BASE_FARE_CENTS) to guard the lower edge of the senior boundary."}],"summary":"The diff is exactly the prescribed minimal fix: a single operator change from > to >= on line 10 of src/fares.ts, plus one new it block in the existing describe('fareFor', ...) in test/fares.test.ts testing age 65 — the exact boundary the ticket targets. No new imports, no new dependencies, no API changes, no unrelated branches altered. All 6 verification criteria are satisfied by the code logic: age 65→175, age 64→350, age 8→175, age 30+pass→0, age 30→350, age 70→175. vitest run passes (5/5 tests, exit 0). tsc --noEmit passes under strict:true (exit 0). The new test would have failed against the pre-fix code (age 65 excluded by > 65, falling through to BASE_FARE_CENTS). No credential-shaped literals in the diff — secrets scan clean. One minor note: age 64 without a pass has no dedicated test, but per blocker discipline this is not a blocker."}
